      "id": "good-strategy-bad-strategy-s012-p01016",
      "source_en": "4. These predictions were described in Pierre Wack, “Scenarios: Uncharted Waters Ahead,” Harvard Business Review, September–October 1985, 73–89. 5. It is difficult to observe this effect in data because few firms are foolish enough to advertise below the threshold. For a very cunning research design that observes a threshold effect in advertising, see Jean-Pierre Dubé, Günter Hitsch, and Puneet Manchanda, “An Empirical Model of Advertising Dynamics,” Quantitative Marketing and Economics 3, no. 2 (2005): 107–44.",
